{
  "summary": "Adds snake_case aliases for options in the `fundrawtransaction` and `walletcreatefundedpsbt` RPCs, updating the RPC schema, client conversions, and documentation. Introduces explicit validation that throws an RPC error if both camelCase and snake_case variants of an option are provided simultaneously, and fixes a bug where `subtract_fee_from_outputs` was silently ignored by the server.",
  "problem": "Wallet funding RPCs handle option names inconsistently across interfaces. The RPC server accepted some snake_case options that `bitcoin-cli` rejected, `subtract_fee_from_outputs` was ignored entirely in favor of only the camelCase variant, and supplying both variants caused one to be silently ignored without warning.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit message fac8ef10f4 and PR description note that 'subtract_fee_from_outputs' was silently ignored by the server, reported by stutxo in PR #35317.",
    "Diff in src/wallet/rpc/spend.cpp confirms `options[\"subtractFeeFromOutputs\"]` was previously accessed directly without checking the snake_case option, whereas `change_address` and `change_position` had ad-hoc checks."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "",
  "changed_since_previous": "Diff and tests are now present; the change implements a helper `GetOptionWithAlias` to reject conflicting aliases and exercises snake_case options in functional tests.",
  "card": "This PR adds missing snake_case aliases (`change_address`, `change_position`, `lock_unspents`, and `subtract_fee_from_outputs`) to the RPC schema, `bitcoin-cli` client table, and documentation for `fundrawtransaction` and `walletcreatefundedpsbt`. It fixes a bug where `subtract_fee_from_outputs` was previously ignored by the server, and errors out when callers pass both camelCase and snake_case versions of an option instead of silently ignoring one.",
  "needs": [],
  "confidence": "high",
  "uncertainties": [],
  "risk": {
    "level": "medium",
    "touches": [
      "rpc_api",
      "wallet"
    ],
    "why": "Mistakes in parsing or validating wallet funding RPC parameters could cause transaction creation to fail or select the wrong change outputs or fee subtraction rules."
  }
}
